  }
}","section":"urn:a-c:project:8ae07eeca101a93be143e873f9d12ab43e316ef0359058c0c9fa71380880d2d5/source/build_tenants/a_c/representation/stdo-v3.0.5-rc.1/source/standards/schemas/product-definition.schema.json#preamble","start_line":1}],"label":"Schema-bound STDO selection"}}}

{"family":"constraints","record":{"applies_to":["urn:a-c:generation:ba37e2825e4e3c758a5cfaec:record:69f73f783b58e9a9c95bb78c6d51bbc1"],"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:ba37e2825e4e3c758a5cfaec:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:ba37e2825e4e3c758a5cfaec:context:source-first-proposal","id":"urn:a-c:generation:ba37e2825e4e3c758a5cfaec:record:f81b2080d11fe5f72f7b775f56f87a88","judgment_kind":"urn:a-c:generation:ba37e2825e4e3c758a5cfaec:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review","kind":"urn:a-c:generation:ba37e2825e4e3c758a5cfaec:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement","latitude_ref":[],"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:ba37e2825e4e3c758a5cfaec:actor:f-p-author","predicate":{"conditions":["World-model work adopts this profile."],"exceptions":[],"grounding":[{"end_line":163,"path":"build_tenants/a_c/representation/stdo-v3.0.5-rc.1/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md","quote":"Its instance premises hold where world-model work is done under this
profile; they are adopted with it and do not follow from the foundations
(P1, P6):

- I1: institutional source systems enact domain function and stay
  sovereign for operational truth; the builder observes them and replaces
  none of them;
- I2: records do not carry their own meaning, and the people who work with
  them already commit to the objects, implicitly in code paths, records
  and workflows, or explicitly in schemas and policy;
- I3: probabilistic systems can propose correspondences across domains,
  and delivery at volume needs deterministic execution;
- I4: some builders work over a representation space in which identity is
  a geometric direction.","section":"urn:a-c:project:8ae07eeca101a93be143e873f9d12ab43e316ef0359058c0c9fa71380880d2d5/source/build_tenants/a_c/representation/stdo-v3.0.5-rc.1/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law","start_line":150}],"statement":"F21 imports F2 transitions/refinement, F3 results, F8 identity, F9 a_c calculus and F12 method binding; similarly spelled profile ledgers/cuts/overlays/treatments/projections are not calculus records by spelling. Adopted, non-foundational premises are I1 source sovereignty/non-replacement, I2 context-dependent records and pre-existing human object commitments, I3 probabilistic correspondence with deterministic volume delivery, I4 some geometric identity spaces. The table attributes consequences as follows: P1/P6+I1/I2→derived semantic truth; P3/P6+F8/I2 and P1 naming→qualified discriminated entity cuts; P4b/P6/P3+I1→recoverable immutable provenance; P1/P4b+F2/F9→declared treatments and traceable subordinate projections; P1/P3+F12→owner-preserving imports and directional specialisation; P6/P5+F3→candidate construct/gate and run-specific falsification; P3/P6/P4b+F9/I4→space-bound, verified, traceable directions; P2/P6/P0+I3→epistemic control and deterministic compilation; P2/P5/P4a→bounded saturation, explicit gaps, sparse publication and authority-preserving composition; P2→bounded proof wedge; P5/P6+F3→predicate-specific result mappings and no result for unrun verification. The source labels P1/P2/P3/P4a/P6 independent, P0 recovered, P4b derived from P0/P2 given non-reacquirable step facts, and P5 derived from P0/P6 given open-world premises. Profile choices include constitutional intents/manifesto/evidence order, entity-cut surfaces and binding, append-only ledger and initial Git publication lane, five treatment fields and preferred projection order, Builder Project narrowing, working refinements/gate, mean-offset methods and exclusions/verification/publication/storage packages,